roaches for Anomaly Detection in IoT Networks: A Survey&#8221; This achievement reflects the strong academic foundation and high-quality research support provided by the CamTech Graduate Program. Empowering future innovators\u2014one paper at a time!<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-88cc81e e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"88cc81e\" data-element_type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-13ccd7b elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"13ccd7b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"640\" height=\"640\" src=\"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-1024x1024.png\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-image-37224\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-1024x1024.png 1024w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-300x300.png 300w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-150x150.png 150w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-768x768.png 768w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-1536x1536.png 1536w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-100x100.png 100w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02-500x500.png 500w, https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/image_2025-08-16_11-21-02.png 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e73a869 elementor-widget elementor-widget-spacer\" data-id=\"e73a869\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"spacer.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer-inner\"><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ceff6c5 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"ceff6c5\" data-element_type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-57153cd elementor-widget elementor-widget-spacer\" data-id=\"57153cd\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"spacer.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer-inner\"><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>School of Graduate Studies The School of Graduate Studies (SGS) at CamTech University has a philosophy deeply rooted in a proactive response to the dynamic challenges facing our world today, particularly in the context of Industry Revolution 4.0 and its environmental and social implications. Positioned strategically, SGS aims to address these complexities through its overarching theme: &#8220;Science, Technology, and Sustainability (STS).&#8221; At the heart of SGS&#8217;s philosophy are three foundational pillars: academic excellence, impacts on career, and community engagement. These pillars serve as guiding principles shaping the core curriculum across all majors, embodying a holistic approach to graduate education. The vision of becoming a leading graduate school in STS is intricately woven into the design of the core curriculum, aligning educational objectives with the broader goal of producing skilled graduates capable of addressing complex issues in sustainable development. The goals and objectives further solidify this philosophy, emphasizing the establishment of SGS as a center for interdisciplinary collaboration and engagement. By offering high-quality master&#8217;s and doctoral programs, fostering diverse perspectives, and prioritizing critical thinking and problem-solving skills, the core curriculum reflects a commitment to nurturing well-rounded individuals poised to make significant contributions in their respective fields. Master&#8217;s and PhD Programs at CamTech &#8211; Artificial Intelligence&#8211; Data Science&#8211; Science and Technology Studies&#8211; Technology Governance&#8211; Technology Management&#8211; Education Technology&#8211; CyberSecurity&#8211; Financial Technology&#8211; Environmental Technology&#8211; Agriculture Technology&#8211; Industrial Technology What type of graduate? Producing graduates who are interdisciplinary experts and effective leaders. Teaching and Learning Philosophy SGS understands the dynamic educational landscape of the 21st century and tailors our curriculum to suit the needs of our graduate students. We place great emphasis on adult education and employ innovative delivery methods, including flipped learning and blended learning methods. Our teaching and learning principles strongly encourage: Involvement: Active participation in planning and evaluation processes. Past Experiences: Leverage previous successes and mistakes for future learning. Relevant Topics: Emphasize immediate relevance and impact. Problem-Centric Learning: Prioritize practical problem-solving over memorization. Graduate programs No. Specialization\/ Majors Level Duration of Study 1 Technology Management Master\u2019s and Doctoral Degree 2 years (Master) 3 years (Doctor) 2 Technology Governance 3 Data Science 4 Artificial Intelligence 5 Cyber Security Master\u2019s Degree No. Majors of Study Tuition Fees\/ Term Tuition Fee\/year 2-year Tuition Fee Term I Term II Term III 1 Technology Management $1,517 $1,517 $1,517 $4,500 $9,000 2 Technology Governance 3 Data Science 4 Artificial Intelligence 5 Cyber Security Note: The tuition fee above is for Cambodian students. For international students, the tuition fee is $ 5, 000 per year. \u00a0 Doctoral Degree No. Majors of Study Tuition Fees\/ Term Tuition Fee\/year 3-year Tuition Fee Term I Term II Term III 1 Technology Management $1,684 $1,684 $1,684 $5,000 $15,000 2 Technology Governance 3 Data Science 4 Artificial Intelligence 5 Cyber Security Note: The tuition fee above is for Cambodian students. For international students, the tuition fee is $ 6, 000 per year. \u00a0 Admission Requirements Master\u2019s Degree Students can be admitted only if they meet all of the following conditions. Hold a bachelor\u2019s degree with a minimum GPA of 3.20 from an accredited educational institution in Cambodia or overseas; Have an English language proficiency score that meets one of the following tests below IELTS with a minimum of 6.0; the writing band must not be less than 6 TOEFL iBT with a minimum of 60 TOEFL PBT with a minimum of 500 CEFE with a minimum of B2; Have a research proposal that can be turned into a thesis; Have a proven track record of publications (if any); Submit two letters of recommendation. At least one of them must come from a university professor. Noteworthy achievements that could contribute to a Recognition of Prior Learning assessment (if any). Doctoral Degree Students can be admitted only if they meet all of the following conditions. Hold a master\u2019s degree with a minimum GPA of 3.50 from an accredited educational institution in Cambodia or overseas; Have an English language proficiency score that meets one of the following tests below \u00a0IELTS with a minimum of 6.5 with no individual band less than 6 TOEFL iBT with a minimum of 80 TOEFL PBT with a minimum of 550 CEFE with a minimum of C1; \u00a0Have a strong research proposal that can be turned into a doctoral dissertation; Have a proven track record of publications (if any) Be accepted by a CamTech doctoral supervisor who will be designated as the student\u2019s principal supervisor; Submit two letters of recommendation. At least one of them must come from a university professor; Noteworthy achievements that could contribute to a Recognition of Prior Learning assessment (if any). Program Schedule The program follows the trimester system, where the academic year is dividedinto three terms. Each term lasts at least 15 weeks. In general, coursework takes upthe first year. Students then take around six additional terms to work on theirthesis and journal publication. In terms of study schedule, the graduate students are expected to study on Friday 1:00 pm \u2013 3:00 pm and 3:30 pm \u2013 5:30 pm Saturday 8:00 am \u2013 12:30 pm and 1:00 pm: 3:30 pm How to apply? Online Application &#8211; Scan QR or https:\/\/ee-eu.kobotoolbox.org\/x\/FaebcANX Contact Dr. Pich PheaktraAssociate Dean of graduate SchoolE-mail: graduateschool@camtech.edu.kh\u00a0\u00a0Phone: +855 78 212 181\/ +855 86 212 181 (Telegram)\u00a0 Click to download all details about Graduate Program Congratulations to Mr. Sayumphu Ros!We are proud to announce that Mr. Sayumphu Ros, a Ph.D. candidate in Science and Technology Studies, has successfully published his research article &#8220;Can Archaeology be a Form of Colonialism? Exploring the Implications of the Actor-Network Theory&#8221; in Heran\u00e7a \u2013 History, Heritage and Culture Journal (Q2 Scopus). Celebrating Excellence in CamTech&#8217;s Graduate Program!Congratulations to Mr. Lim Kimsreng, a Master\u2019s student in the Cybersecurity Program, School of Graduate Studies, CamTech University, for successfully presenting his research at the IEEE Conference at SKIMA 2025 in the UK. Research Title: &#8220;Machine Learning Approaches for Anomaly Detection in IoT Networks: A Survey&#8221; This achievement reflects the strong academic foundation and high-quality research support provided by the CamTech Graduate Program. [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"elementor_header_footer","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-15608","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry","post-no-thumbnail"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/15608","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/4"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=15608"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/15608\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":39240,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/15608\/revisions\/39240"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=15608"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}